D2  Decentralisation WITHOUT insurance  (Section 8.2.2, Eq. 94)
==============================================================================
Same prices, no insurance market. Eq. (94) requires every agent's CVaR
multiplier to equal the planner's; with heterogeneous exposures it cannot.
We measure the resulting dispersion and the allocation error.
  max_k max_w |gamma_k(w) - gamma(w)| = 1.509819e-02
  mean over agents                    = 1.170490e-02
  >> Eq. (94) FAILS without insurance
  max_k |allocation_k - planner_k|    = 2.187221e+02
  per-agent tail-scenario counts: min=21, max=29, planner=25
  (differing tail sets across agents is precisely the obstruction in 8.2.2)

